+| No Unreal tools in Codex | Direct/proxy config missing, client catalog stale, or project config not trusted | Inspect active config and both connection names with `codex mcp list`; follow proxy recovery before concluding the editor is stopped. |
+| Endpoint not reachable | Editor not running, plugin disabled, server not started, or wrong endpoint/project | Inspect startup logs, port ownership, and configured URL; start the verified editor/server when authorized. |
+| Server responds but has no domain tools | Tool providers not enabled | Enable `AllToolsets` or the intended individual toolset plugins in addition to `ModelContextProtocol`. |
 | Port bind failure | Another local service owns the port | Start with another port, update `ServerPortNumber`, regenerate/merge Codex config. |
 | Only meta-tools are visible | Normal tool-search mode | Use `list_toolsets`, `describe_toolset`, `call_tool`. Do not expect every domain tool in the native tool list. |
 | Expected domain toolset is missing | Plugin disabled or registry cache stale | Enable the related UE plugin if required, restart if needed, run `ModelContextProtocol.RefreshTools`. |
-| Tool call hangs | Editor is compiling, loading, in modal UI, or receiving overlapping calls | Wait, avoid parallel calls, check compilation/PIE state, restart server if needed. |
+| Tool call hangs | Editor compiling/loading, modal UI, or conflicting calls | Check compile/PIE state and dependencies. For an authorized live C++ rebuild discover `LiveCodingToolset.CompileLiveCoding` and await its result. Never replay a mutation whose outcome is unknown. |
 | Blueprint/material/widget operation returns odd data | PIE/editor mode mismatch or compile failed | Stop PIE, inspect returned status/logs, compile again only after identifying the failing path. |
 | New C++ tool does not appear | Reflection schema did not reload | Restart editor after adding reflected declarations. |
+| Concurrent calls conflict | Shared state or asynchronous completion ordering | Serialize dependent calls and same-state mutations; only supported independent calls may overlap. Coordinate agents. |
